{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:693c559e842aadf93ddcaba5f140c97aac1419c23fda3c1038c7a690c13b1213", "sample_idx": 25, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3.5-397b-a17b", "content": "Section 1\nThe Guardian has issued a series of clarifications regarding recent reporting errors found in various articles published on August 25 and in the preceding week. These corrections address factual inaccuracies spanning legal jurisdictions, corporate titles, personal names, religious affiliations, and historical family relationships. The newspaper aims to ensure that readers possess the correct information regarding these specific stories by explicitly amending the original claims made in print and online formats.\n\nSection 2\n* One major correction clarifies that the new legislation criminalizing the abduction of cats and dogs as a specific offence applies only to England and Northern Ireland, rather than the entire United Kingdom as previously stated, while also correcting the title of Eileen Burbidge at Fertifa from founder to executive director, noting that Tony Chen and Nick Kuan are the actual founders of the reproductive health benefit scheme company.\n* Additional amendments fix the surname of director Alex Lawther in an interview with Juliet Stevenson, correct the religious background of the family in Bend It Like Beckham from Muslim to Sikh, and clarify that it was the third Baron Stanley, not the fourth, who converted to Islam in the context of Venetia Stanley's relationship with Prime Minister Herbert Asquith, alongside a list of other recently updated articles covering topics from Pavel Durov's arrest to royal servants.\n\n***\n\nThe publication invites further correspondence from readers who wish to discuss these amendments or raise new concerns directly with the Readers' Editor. Contact details provided include a physical mailing address at York Way in London, a dedicated email address for the Observer, and a telephone number to facilitate direct communication regarding editorial standards and accuracy.\n\nSection 3\nThese corrections highlight the importance of precision in journalism, especially when dealing with sensitive topics such as criminal law, corporate leadership, and religious identity. By acknowledging these mistakes openly, the newspaper demonstrates a commitment to maintaining trust with its audience and upholding high standards of factual integrity across its diverse range of coverage.\n\nSection 4\nReaders are encouraged to review the amended articles online or in future editions to access the verified information. The list of corrected pieces serves as a transparent record of the newspaper's ongoing efforts to rectify errors and provide the most accurate news possible to the public community.\n\nP.P.S This summary encompasses all the specific corrections and contact information detailed in the original notice.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Section", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " ", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -2.121948e-05}, {"token": " Guardian", "logprob": -0.039602667}, {"token": " has", "logprob": -0.04393219}, {"token": " issued", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " a", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " series", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " clar", "logprob": -0.45865262}, {"token": "ifications", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " regarding", "logprob": -0.39848945}, {"token": " recent", "logprob": -8.3446537e-07}, {"token": " reporting", "logprob": -0.0018785348}, {"token": " errors", "logprob": -1.192093e-07}, {"token": " found", "logprob": -0.00038684937}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.00011110923}, {"token": " various", "logprob": -0.00017805492}, {"token": " articles", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " published", "logprob": -0.002796324}, {"token": " on", "logprob": -0.02101498}, {"token": " August", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " ", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "2", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "5", "